    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d358-a9">

                <pb facs="0385" n="325" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg325"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 9 in No. 88—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Captain Kiesel to Mr. Wetter</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Division Navale de l’Océan Indien,<lb/>Aviso de</hi> l<hi
                                rendition="#superscript">re</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">classe Le Papni, commandant</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Bord, le</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-03-24"><hi rendition="#italic">24 mars
                                1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have been officially notified that the judgment returned against J. Waller, an
                    American subject, by the council of war sitting at Tamatave has been carried
                    out. <pb facs="0386" n="326" xml:id="pg326"/> Referring to your letter No. 214,
                    I have immediately requested an authentic copy of the judgment, and have the
                    honor to inclose it herewith.</p>
                <p>Will you accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. N. Kiesel</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
